' 01 Components of Reified RSpaces: the modules of every phase, the storage
' substrate of phase P1 in detail, and the host that they call.
'
' Source of Figure S1 in ../design.md (section S1). The figure restates the
' module map of design part N1 (Table N1.1) and the files of the later
' phases: the syntax layer models/src/rust/reified/ and the normalizer arms
' (P2, P3), rholang/src/rust/interpreter/reified/ and spaces/ (P4 to P9),
' tensor/ (P6), the substrate files rspace++/src/rspace/space_store_handle.rs,
' rspace/space_play.rs and replay_rspace/space_replay.rs (P1), and the native
' backend replay_rspace/native_session/space.rs with the accessor space_store
' (decision 47). It adds no new fact.
'
' Changed by decisions 98, 109 and 114: the node setup installs the
' VectorDB services of a validator, a play publishes the batch of each
' commit, and nothing repairs the mirror. Before, the node setup started
' the mirror reconciler, and the final result of an evaluation settled its
' mirror journal.
'
' Reading order, from the top to the bottom:
'   1. The callers: a deploy program, the code of a user agent (P8), Casper,
'      which evaluates each deploy and never changes, and the node setup,
'      which installs the VectorDB services of a validator (P6).
'   2. The frontend: the parser, the normalizer arms and the syntax layer
'      turn the source text into a Par with the fields of each construct (P2, P3).
'   3. The interpreter at the baseline with its hook lines: the reducer and
'      the runtime constructors.
'   4. The Reified runtime: the routing, the scheduling, the system
'      processes, the translation of user agents, the Seq rules, the costs,
'      and the VectorDB services.
'   5. The spaces: the agent and its engine, the disciplines, the outer
'      stores, the records, the theories, the factory, the mirror capture,
'      and the exact numbers.
'   6. The substrate of P1. The handle opens a HostTxn through the
'      SpaceTxnHost trait. The HostTxn holds the staging core, and its commit
'      runs each operation through the backend of its mode.
'   7. The mode backends: the child modules of P1, and the native backend of
'      decision 47.
'   8. The host at the baseline, which the substrate calls and never changes,
'      with the hot store and the history trie under it, and the external
'      services of the VectorDB mirror.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 01-substrate-components.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 01-substrate-components
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam PackageBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ComponentBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 50
title Components of Reified RSpaces: the modules of every phase, the substrate of P1 in detail, and the host that they call

package "Callers" as CALLERS $rrs_host {
  component PROGRAM $rrs_syntax [
  **Deploy program**
  Rholang source text with
  Reified syntax
  ]
  component USERCODE $rrs_agent [
  **Code of a user agent** (P8)
  an ordinary Rholang program
  that serves gensym, produce, consume
  ]
  component CASPER $rrs_host [
  **Casper** (casper/src unchanged)
  RuntimeManager plays and replays
  each deploy; spaces enter a block
  through its post-state root
  ]
  component NODE $rrs_host [
  **Node setup**
  node/src/rust/runtime/setup.rs:
  installs the VectorDB services (P6)
  ]
}

package "Frontend: source text to Par (P2, P3)" as FRONTEND $rrs_syntax {
  component PARSER $rrs_syntax [
  **Parser v3** (rholang-rs,
  feature/reified-rspaces-v3)
  tree-sitter grammar and scanner:
  use, free, params, queries, floats
  ]
  component NORMALIZERS $rrs_syntax [
  **Normalizer arms**
  compiler/normalizer/processes/:
  p_use_block, p_free_theory,
  reified_syntax, and the arms of
  send, sync send, input and new
  ]
  component SYNTAX $rrs_syntax [
  **Syntax layer** models/src/rust/reified/
  encoding, builders, params, query_spec,
  validation: the fields use_blocks, space_types,
  params, query_spec and EFree (decision 112)
  models/src/rust/space_factory_urn.rs:
  the families, URNs and aliases
  ]
}

package "Interpreter at the baseline, with hook lines (P2, P4, P7)" as INTERP $rrs_host {
  component REDUCER $rrs_host [
  **Reducer** reduce.rs, util/mod.rs
  hooks H2 to H4, receive, new, the
  root evaluation
  ]
  component RHORUNTIME $rrs_host [
  **Runtime constructors** rho_runtime.rs
  the Reified definitions, the bound
  SpaceTxnHost, the native bind call;
  system_processes.rs: embed and ann are recorded
  ]
}

package "Reified runtime: rholang/src/rust/interpreter/reified/ (P4 to P9)" as REIFIED $rrs_name {
  component ROUTE $rrs_name [
  **Hooks, routing and scope**
  reducer_hooks.rs, route.rs, scope.rs,
  execution.rs (the R7 backend): routes R1
  to R7, space references, the use context,
  params and queries
  ]
  component SCHED $rrs_name [
  **Runtime**
  runtime.rs: each space job runs inline
  in the counted task of its caller,
  the modes of the runtime, the scope
  of a root evaluation and its sweep
  ]
  component SYSPROC $rrs_system [
  **System processes**
  system_channels.rs, system_processes.rs,
  factory.rs, handle.rs: factories,
  HANDLE_OP, getSpaceAgent, assertEqual,
  rho:lang:vector
  ]
  component USERAGENT $rrs_name [
  **User agents** user_agent.rs
  translation of new, send, receive;
  MATCHER_OP and SINK_OP (P8)
  ]
  component SEQ $rrs_name [
  **Seq send rule** seq.rs
  SQ-1 and SQ-2: the scan
  of each send (P7)
  ]
  component COSTS $rrs_name [
  **Costs and errors**
  costs.rs, errors.rs
  FIRE_ROUND_CAP and the fire rounds
  ]
  component VDBSVC $rrs_service [
  **VectorDB services**
  vectordb_services.rs: the embedder,
  the mirror and its writer (P6)
  ]
}

package "Spaces: rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/ and tensor/ (P4 to P7)" as SPACES $rrs_agent {
  component AGENT $rrs_agent [
  **Space agent and engine**
  agent.rs, generic.rs, join.rs, settle.rs,
  matching.rs, families.rs: reads the
  staged view, decides each outcome,
  stages whole operations, and commits
  ]
  component DISC $rrs_agent [
  **Disciplines** disciplines/
  bag, set, cell, queue, stack,
  priority_queue, vectordb, scan
  ]
  component OUTER $rrs_agent [
  **Outer stores** outer/ and pathmap/
  hashmap, array, vector, hashset,
  pathmap: adapter, path codec, re-rooting,
  markers, delivery, prefix joins
  ]
  component RECORDS $rrs_agent [
  **Records, ids and claims**
  record.rs, counter.rs, allocator.rs,
  namespace.rs, types/; ephemeral.rs:
  volatile ids and the Seq claims (SQ-3)
  ]
  component FACTORY $rrs_factory [
  **Factory** factory/
  urn, constructor, defaults:
  the nine gates
  ]
  component THEORY $rrs_checker [
  **Theories** theory/
  builtin, identity:
  admission fails closed
  ]
  component MIRROR $rrs_service [
  **Mirror capture** mirror.rs
  the net writes of a commit
  ]
  component TENSOR $rrs_system [
  **Exact numbers** tensor/
  num, exact, ops, costs (P6)
  ]
}

package "Substrate of P1: rspace++/src/rspace/space_store_handle.rs" as SUB $rrs_substrate {
  component HANDLE $rrs_substrate [
  **SpaceStoreHandle** (one for each host)
  shared HandleState: the open contexts of
  transactions and sweeps (FR-9, FR-9'), and the
  committed parent orders of the scope (FR-5')
  ]
  component HOSTTRAIT $rrs_substrate [
  **trait SpaceTxnHost<C, P, A, K>**
  mode, matcher, begin,
  root_leaf_record_count, sweep_volatile
  ]
  component TXN $rrs_substrate [
  **HostTxn**: the SpaceTxn of every mode
  reads: data, continuations, joins,
  produce_counters, recorded_comms, admits
  staging: produce, consume
  commit: the single mutation point
  ]
  component CORE $rrs_substrate [
  **TxnCore**
  staged view TxnView, keyed by the store identity
  <latex>\mathrm{key}(c) = \mathrm{Blake2b256}(\mathrm{bincode}(c))</latex> (FR-2)
  counter view <latex>\kappa_v(p) = \kappa_{\mathrm{host}}(p) + \delta(p)</latex>
  LockCoverage (FR-4) and the installed guard
  paired COMM events (replay and reporting)
  staged operations with their staged effects
  ]
  ' Changed by decision 90 (DR-132): no production caller installs an order scope. The text before:
  '   operation i under <latex>\mathit{parent} \mathbin{+\!\!+} [(i, 2)]</latex>
  component COMMIT $rrs_substrate [
  **commit_staged**
  each operation i, under <latex>\mathit{parent} \mathbin{+\!\!+} [(i, 2)]</latex>
  only when a test installs an order scope
  read-only checks, host calls,
  and the event correlation (FR-7')
  ]
  component SWEEP $rrs_substrate [
  **sweep_volatile_channels**
  read-only validation, then the removal
  of continuations, joins, and data,
  with no event and no observer call
  ]
}

package "Mode backends (child modules of the hosts)" as BACKENDS $rrs_substrate {
  component PLAY $rrs_substrate [
  **PlayBackend**: rspace/space_play.rs
  the play call order of ops_produce.rs
  and ops_consume.rs (legacy and native play)
  ]
  component REPLAY $rrs_substrate [
  **ReplayBackend**: replay_rspace/space_replay.rs
  the replay call order of replay_rspace.rs,
  and a directive fails closed
  ]
  component NATIVE $rrs_substrate [
  **NativeSpaceHost** (decision 47)
  replay_rspace/native_session/space.rs:
  each operation meets its journal row
  through the ticket protocol
  ]
}

package "Host at the baseline (unchanged code)" as HOST $rrs_host {
  component RSPACE $rrs_host [
  **RSpace** (play)
  log_*, produce_counters, observe_*,
  start_accounting_operation, wrap_result
  ]
  component REPLAYSPACE $rrs_host [
  **ReplayRSpace** (replay)
  counter increment and rollback,
  store_*, remove_bindings_for, wrap_result
  ]
  component REPORTING $rrs_host [
  **ReportingRspace** (reporting)
  an inner replay space
  with the ReportingLogger
  ]
  component SESSION $rrs_host [
  **Native replay session**
  native_session.rs and the accounting
  module, with the one accessor
  space_store (decision 47), which
  rho_runtime.rs binds (W3)
  ]
  component LOCKS $rrs_host [
  **Lock stripes**
  consume_lock: phase A, then phase B,
  each in ascending index order
  ]
  component OBSERVER $rrs_host [
  **Accounting observer**
  start, produce or consume,
  COMM, and finish
  ]
  component EVENTS $rrs_host [
  **Event log** (play)
  grouped and sorted
  by operation order
  ]
  component REPLAYDATA $rrs_host [
  **Replay table** (replay)
  the bindings that rig
  builds from the play log
  ]
}

database "Hot store\n(hot_store.rs)" as HOT $rrs_storage
database "History trie" as HIST $rrs_storage
component CHROMA $rrs_service [
**ChromaDB service** and
the **embedder** (SBERT):
local to one node, outside
every state root
]

note right of HIST
**Unchanged at the baseline**
ISpace, ispace_impl.rs, hot_store.rs,
trace, serializers, history, merger,
contract_call.rs, dispatch.rs, every
.proto file, and casper/src
end note

' Horizontal order inside the layers.
SEQ -[hidden]right-> USERAGENT
USERAGENT -[hidden]right-> SCHED
SCHED -[hidden]right-> COSTS
COSTS -[hidden]right-> VDBSVC
AGENT -[hidden]right-> FACTORY
DISC -[hidden]right-> OUTER
OUTER -[hidden]right-> RECORDS
RECORDS -[hidden]right-> THEORY
THEORY -[hidden]right-> MIRROR
RSPACE -[hidden]down-> LOCKS
EVENTS -[hidden]down-> HOT

' Callers, frontend and interpreter.
PROGRAM -[$rrs_flow]-> PARSER : source text
PARSER -[$rrs_flow]right-> NORMALIZERS : syntax tree
NORMALIZERS -[$rrs_flow]right-> SYNTAX : builders\nand validators
NORMALIZERS -[$rrs_flow]-> RHORUNTIME : normalized Par\nwith its fields
CASPER -[$rrs_flow]-> RHORUNTIME : play and replay\nof each deploy
RHORUNTIME -[$rrs_flow]-> REDUCER : evaluates the term

' Reified runtime.
REDUCER -[$rrs_flow]-> ROUTE : hooks
REDUCER -[$rrs_flow]-> SYSPROC : calls on op channels\nand handles
USERCODE -[$rrs_flow]-> SYSPROC : MATCHER_OP, SINK_OP,\nhandle calls
NODE -[$rrs_flow]-> VDBSVC : installs the services\nof a validator
ROUTE -[$rrs_flow]-> SEQ : scan of a send
ROUTE -[$rrs_flow]-> USERAGENT : agent route
ROUTE -[$rrs_flow]-> SCHED : space operation,\nroot evaluation
USERCODE <-[$rrs_flow]- USERAGENT : gensym, produce\nand consume calls
SYSPROC -[$rrs_flow]-> SCHED : factory and\nhandle jobs
SYSPROC -[$rrs_flow]-> VDBSVC : embed, ann

' Spaces.
SCHED -[$rrs_flow]-> AGENT : runs each job\ninline
SYSPROC -[$rrs_relation]-> FACTORY : constructor
COSTS <-[$rrs_relation]- AGENT : the fire rounds
AGENT -[$rrs_relation]-> DISC : candidate order
AGENT -[$rrs_relation]-> OUTER : keys and paths
AGENT -[$rrs_relation]-> RECORDS : envelopes, counters,\nSeq claims
AGENT -[$rrs_relation]-> THEORY : admission
AGENT -[$rrs_effect]-> MIRROR : the receipt\nof each commit
VDBSVC <-[$rrs_flow]- MIRROR : the batch of each\ncommit in play (run_op)
VDBSVC -[$rrs_flow]right-> CHROMA : mirror writes,\nqueries, embeddings
DISC -[$rrs_relation]-> TENSOR : exact scores
SYSPROC -[$rrs_relation]-> TENSOR : rho:lang:vector

' Substrate, backends and host.
AGENT -[$rrs_flow]-> HANDLE : begin(lock keys)
SCHED -[$rrs_flow]-> HANDLE : begin_evaluation_scope()\nsweep_volatile(channels)
HANDLE -[$rrs_flow]right-> HOSTTRAIT : begin(lock keys, registration)\nsweep_volatile(channels, registration)
HOSTTRAIT -[$rrs_flow]-> TXN : opens
HOSTTRAIT -[$rrs_flow]-> SWEEP : sweep
AGENT -[$rrs_flow]-> TXN : reads, stages, commits
TXN *-[$rrs_relation]- CORE
TXN -[$rrs_flow]-> COMMIT : commit()
COMMIT -[$rrs_flow]-> PLAY : apply_op (play)
COMMIT -[$rrs_flow]-> REPLAY : apply_op (replay, reporting)
COMMIT -[$rrs_flow]-> NATIVE : apply_op (native replay)
PLAY -[$rrs_effect]-> RSPACE : host calls
REPLAY -[$rrs_effect]-> REPLAYSPACE : host calls
NATIVE -[$rrs_effect]-> SESSION : tickets and\njournal rows
HOSTTRAIT <|.[$rrs_relation]. RSPACE : implements
HOSTTRAIT <|.[$rrs_relation]. REPLAYSPACE : implements
HOSTTRAIT <|.[$rrs_relation]. REPORTING : implements
HOSTTRAIT <|.[$rrs_relation]. NATIVE : implements
REPORTING -[$rrs_relation]left-> REPLAYSPACE : delegates
RSPACE -[$rrs_relation]-> LOCKS : begin takes
REPLAYSPACE -[$rrs_relation]-> LOCKS : begin takes
RSPACE -[$rrs_relation]-> OBSERVER
REPLAYSPACE -[$rrs_relation]-> OBSERVER
RSPACE -[$rrs_effect]-> EVENTS : logs
REPLAYSPACE -[$rrs_relation]-> REPLAYDATA : verify reads,\ncommit removes bindings
RSPACE -[$rrs_effect]-> HOT
REPLAYSPACE -[$rrs_effect]-> HOT
SESSION -[$rrs_effect]-> HOT
CORE -[$rrs_relation]-> HOT : loads lists\n(read-through)
SWEEP -[$rrs_effect]-> HOT : removes the volatile state
HOT -[$rrs_relation]-> HIST : reads through,\nthe checkpoint writes

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_syntax>     | syntax: the source text, the parser, the normalizer arms and the syntax layer |
|<$rrs_host>       | code at the baseline: unchanged, or changed only by hook lines |
|<$rrs_name>       | Reified runtime: routing, scheduling, translation, Seq rules and costs (new code) |
|<$rrs_system>     | system processes and the exact numbers that they use (new code) |
|<$rrs_agent>      | space agents and their parts, and the code of a user agent |
|<$rrs_factory>    | factory |
|<$rrs_service>    | services outside consensus: the VectorDB services, the mirror, ChromaDB |
|<$rrs_substrate>  | substrate of P1 and its mode backends (new code) |
|<$rrs_storage>    | stored state: hot store and history trie |
**Arrows**
|<$rrs_flow>       | call or input |
|<$rrs_effect>     | effect on the stored state |
|<$rrs_relation>   | relation |
endlegend
@enduml
